1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,090
I know that you were hurt when I left you.

6
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,600
I had no choice.

7
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:21,080
Don’t be sad, Chan.

8
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,990
I want to be by your side
and take care of you for a long time.

9
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,820
If you kiss me
and you don’t feel that excitement,

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,010
I will let you go.

11
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:30,420
Key.

12
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,500
Key, wait.

13
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:33,370
Every time I kiss you.

14
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,210
My heart is always beating fast.

15
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:36,840
It happens only with you.

16
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:47,500
We met before?

17
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:53,700
Yes.

18
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:56,170
When I was 15.

19
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:00,910
I’m sorry.

20
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,630
I don’t remember it.

21
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:05,800
It’s okay.

22
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:09,400
It happened ten years ago.

23
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,240
It’s not surprising that you forgot it.

24
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,100
But you remember me.

25
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,200
You’ve never forgotten me.

26
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,500
You can be mad at me.

27
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,200
I forgot something this important.

28
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:31,329
I deserve it.

29
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,350
Fine.

30
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:39,200
I admit that I’m a little upset about it.

31
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,500
But I’m more upset
when I saw you kiss another woman.

32
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:53,100
I’m sorry.

33
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,700
Your apology is not enough.

34
00:03:03,690 --> 00:03:04,900
What do I need to do?

35
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:07,100
So you will stop being mad at me.

36
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,300
There’s actually a way.

37
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,000
Tonight.

38
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:24,480
I’ll be the only one who can kiss you.

39
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:28,780
You can’t kiss me

40
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:32,000
without my permission.

41
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,290
Is this your way of getting back at me?

42
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,400
Will you agree to it?

43
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:45,700
Fine.

44
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:48,500
From now on,

45
00:03:49,329 --> 00:03:50,900
I’ll let you have your way.

46
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,500
Then I won’t hold back.

47
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,450
I have something important to tell you.

48
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:22,780
I want to cancel our deal.

49
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,900
I don’t want you…

50
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:37,100
to be my sugar baby anymore.

51
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:43,600
Key.

52
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,200
Will you be my girlfriend?

53
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,400
Yes.

54
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:09,040
I have wanted to be your girlfriend
for a long time.

55
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:13,470
So you are now my girlfriend.

56
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:23,570
Hey.

57
00:05:25,690 --> 00:05:26,800
Don’t forget.

58
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:29,000
You can’t kiss me

59
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,600
without my permission.

60
00:05:40,490 --> 00:05:41,300
Fine.

61
00:05:41,790 --> 00:05:44,900
♪ Just hold my gaze a little longer ♪

62
00:05:45,090 --> 00:05:47,600
♪ Move your heart a little closer ♪

63
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:52,100
♪ Let’s take the meaning of love
a little further ♪

64
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:55,700
♪ What we have doesn't end tonight ♪

65
00:05:56,409 --> 00:05:57,820
Don’t play dumb.

66
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,580
I can’t help it. I’m used to it.

67
00:06:02,510 --> 00:06:05,630
♪ I’ll make you love me,
make you remember ♪

68
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:08,700
♪ I’ll keep repeating till you surrender ♪

69
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:12,600
♪ With every touch, remember only me ♪

70
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:16,100
♪ I’ll hold you close in everything I do ♪

71
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:19,190
♪ Make it sink in, make you remember too ♪

72
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:20,800
That’s cheating.

73
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:24,920
Let’s go back to my room.

74
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,770
As we have agreed.

75
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,450
Tonight,

76
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,300
I’m the only one who can kiss you.

77
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,500
You can’t kiss me

78
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,800
without my permission.

79
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:50,080
Will you be my girlfriend?

80
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:52,100
Yes.

81
00:11:11,370 --> 00:11:12,300
Miss Chan.

82
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:13,520
Mr. Phu wants to see you.

83
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:15,330
Send him in.

84
00:11:20,470 --> 00:11:21,300
Please come in.

85
00:11:22,410 --> 00:11:23,250
Thank you.

86
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:30,000
Chan.

87
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:31,750
Morning, Phu.

88
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:38,200
Chan.

89
00:11:39,090 --> 00:11:40,300
Are you okay?

90
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,800
I’m fine.

91
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:45,100
Why?

92
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:46,100
No.

93
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:48,100
This is not normal.

94
00:11:49,290 --> 00:11:51,040
You said ‘Good morning’ to me.

95
00:11:51,230 --> 00:11:52,400
You also smile.

96
00:11:52,770 --> 00:11:54,400
You barely smile to anyone.

97
00:11:55,790 --> 00:11:59,130
From now on, I’ll smile more often.

98
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:02,370
You are in such a good mood.

99
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:05,290
Because Jay
checked out of the hotel, right?

100
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:10,100
Jay told you that?

101
00:12:10,990 --> 00:12:11,800
Yes.

102
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,770
She also asked me to tell you

103
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,400
that she would keep her word.

104
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,650
That’s all?

105
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:20,450
Yes.

106
00:12:23,050 --> 00:12:25,900
Right, the money that I owed Jay.

107
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:28,290
I almost paid it all back.

108
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:30,800
I got money from my dad.

109
00:12:31,130 --> 00:12:34,780
You don’t need to worry
that Jay will ask me to do something.

110
00:12:35,510 --> 00:12:37,130
I will cut ties with her.

111
00:12:39,510 --> 00:12:40,600
Thank you, Phu.

112
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:42,700
Thank me?

113
00:12:43,010 --> 00:12:46,400
I should be the one who thanks you
for not ending our friendship.

114
00:12:47,690 --> 00:12:49,300
If I cut you off,

115
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:51,100
I would have no friends left.

116
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,000
I still feel guilty anyway.

117
00:12:57,070 --> 00:12:58,270
I’m sorry, Chan.

118
00:13:00,470 --> 00:13:01,300
Forget it.

119
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:02,700
It’s in the past now.

120
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:06,000
But you need to promise me.

121
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:09,600
From now on, if you have a problem,

122
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,570
you need to tell me.

123
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,600
Don’t be afraid to ask for my help.

124
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:15,600
Get it?

125
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:17,500
Yes.

126
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:19,900
I promise.

127
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:28,100
Phu.

128
00:13:29,210 --> 00:13:33,000
You told me you have a friend
who is a tattoo artist, right?

129
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,800
He did tattoos for many celebrities.

130
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,200
Yes.

131
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,000
Why?

132
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:53,300
Is it heavy? Let me help you.

133
00:13:54,670 --> 00:13:57,580
I won’t come to meet you
before our performance tomorrow.

134
00:13:57,910 --> 00:13:59,900
I’ll send you the setlist.

135
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:02,300
I’ll go meet you at the Crescent.

136
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:05,500
Our frontman flakes on us again.

137
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:08,000
I have a matter to tend to.

138
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:09,690
What matter?

139
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,980
A matter of the heart?

140
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,100
I knew it.

141
00:14:14,450 --> 00:14:15,930
Key is in such a good mood today.

142
00:14:15,970 --> 00:14:17,300
She only sang love songs today.

143
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:19,950
When we were going to play a sad song,
she told us to play other songs.

144
00:14:19,990 --> 00:14:20,800
You’re right.

145
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:23,510
A few days ago,
you were moping around like a sad puppy.

146
00:14:23,550 --> 00:14:24,700
What’s going on?

147
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:25,800
Spill it.

148
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:28,500
Nothing is going on.

149
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:30,310
I just…

150
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:33,900
I…

151
00:14:34,370 --> 00:14:35,210
I have a girlfriend.

152
00:14:35,690 --> 00:14:36,800
Damn!

153
00:14:38,370 --> 00:14:40,600
Why are you that surprised?

154
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:43,130
I didn’t mishear it, right?

155
00:14:43,470 --> 00:14:44,860
I can’t believe it.

156
00:14:45,110 --> 00:14:48,200
Key has stopped flirting around.

157
00:14:48,550 --> 00:14:49,400
Yeah.

158
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:53,400
Didn’t you say you didn’t want
to be in a relationship?

159
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,590
I said that because
I’ve been waiting for her.

160
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:58,450
All my life,
I will be committed only to her.

161
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:02,380
Her? Who is she?

162
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,440
Let me see her picture.

163
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,780
-Come on. Let us see it.
-Let us see it.

164
00:15:05,810 --> 00:15:07,960
-Grab her.
-No.

165
00:15:07,980 --> 00:15:09,450
-Come on. Let us see her picture.
-No.

166
00:15:09,470 --> 00:15:11,130
-Show it to us.
-No.

167
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:12,070
We won’t tell anyone.

168
00:15:12,090 --> 00:15:13,180
No.

169
00:15:33,810 --> 00:15:35,100
What are you doing here?

170
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,000
I came to pick you up.

171
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,290
You don’t work today, do you?

172
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:41,800
Yes.

173
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:44,000
We just finished our practice.

174
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:45,610
We’re about to go home.

175
00:15:47,990 --> 00:15:53,400
Miss Chan, you and Key…

176
00:15:58,540 --> 00:15:59,570
We are dating.

177
00:16:00,950 --> 00:16:02,670
They are dating.

178
00:16:03,580 --> 00:16:04,700
You are dating?

179
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:12,500
Come on.

180
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:13,890
Let’s go home, sweetie.

181
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,700
I’ll help you carry it.

182
00:16:18,390 --> 00:16:19,170
Yes.

183
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:20,650
Honey.

184
00:16:28,690 --> 00:16:29,550
Let’s go.

185
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:32,200
Are you leaving?

186
00:16:38,650 --> 00:16:39,600
Get in.

187
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:46,690
She suddenly acts all needy.

188
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,770
What’s the occasion?

189
00:17:30,370 --> 00:17:31,300
It…

190
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:34,300
It’s a very special occasion.

191
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,200
Our anniversary?

192
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:41,610
I don’t think so.

193
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:45,100
Did something good happen to you?

194
00:17:46,490 --> 00:17:50,200
Let’s say it’s something
you’d never expect.

195
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:53,100
So…

196
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:55,600
What do I need to do for you to tell me?

197
00:17:58,010 --> 00:17:59,570
Do you really want to know it?

198
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,700
Yes.

199
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:08,100
Can you help me take my jacket off?

200
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:12,300
You are acting strange today.

201
00:18:33,850 --> 00:18:34,780
So?

202
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,500
Can you tell me now?

203
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:40,500
Don’t you notice anything?

204
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:43,450
Any changes in me?

205
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:52,600
You got a tattoo?

206
00:18:54,650 --> 00:18:55,820
Keep your voice down.

207
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:57,310
You’re startling others.

208
00:18:59,630 --> 00:19:03,700
Did you get the treble clef tattoo for me?

209
00:19:04,530 --> 00:19:05,330
Yes.

210
00:19:06,570 --> 00:19:07,800
This time,

211
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:10,500
I will remember you.

212
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:15,100
To tell you the truth,

213
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,300
the tattoo has another meaning.

214
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:20,500
When we write a song,

215
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:25,960
the first thing we write
is the treble clef.

216
00:19:28,670 --> 00:19:30,600
It’s the beginning of everything.

217
00:19:33,290 --> 00:19:34,530
Just like you.

218
00:19:38,740 --> 00:19:40,700
You are a new beginning for me.

219
00:19:42,810 --> 00:19:45,100
Because of you,
I want to start singing again.

220
00:19:52,470 --> 00:19:53,980
The tattoo,

221
00:19:55,130 --> 00:19:56,250
are you sure about it?

222
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,030
Why?

223
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:02,200
You also have a tattoo.

224
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,180
I think this tattoo looks great.

225
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:14,800
Won’t your family be against it?

226
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:17,170
One more thing.

227
00:20:19,410 --> 00:20:23,850
It might not look good
for an executive like you.

228
00:20:25,010 --> 00:20:26,500
Managing the business,

229
00:20:27,910 --> 00:20:29,300
I use my brain.

230
00:20:30,590 --> 00:20:32,370
It has nothing to do with my tattoo.

231
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,500
About my family,

232
00:20:35,090 --> 00:20:37,100
I don’t think
they will have a problem with it.

233
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:38,400
I’m an adult.

234
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:41,200
My body, my choice.

235
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:46,400
No one will judge me
because of the tattoo.

236
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:53,900
Thank you for doing this for me.

237
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:57,700
From now on,

238
00:20:58,730 --> 00:21:00,600
I will do everything only for you.

239
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,800
You are crazy in love.

240
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:14,100
I like this side of you.

241
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:30,700
This is the first time
that I’m late to work.

242
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,200
You are only a few minutes late.

243
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,600
I always come to work early.

244
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:39,000
But you can’t blame me.

245
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:40,890
You were the one who wouldn’t go to sleep.

246
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:46,290
How could I go to sleep
when you wore that nightgown?

247
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,100
Did you like it?

248
00:21:52,130 --> 00:21:53,100
Yes.

249
00:21:54,340 --> 00:21:55,890
Then stop complaining.

250
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:59,600
But you need to stop
distracting me from work.

251
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,180
Do you get it, stubborn kid?

252
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:05,000
I got it.

253
00:22:06,410 --> 00:22:07,600
You should go to work.

254
00:22:08,010 --> 00:22:09,500
I’ll hang around to wait for you.

255
00:22:09,650 --> 00:22:11,000
Let’s have lunch together.

256
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,410
Lunch?

257
00:22:12,690 --> 00:22:13,600
Yes.

258
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:15,580
I know a restaurant
serving delicious food.

259
00:22:15,650 --> 00:22:17,200
It also has a nice atmosphere.

260
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,780
Can I have a rain check?

261
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,800
I have a meeting today.

262
00:22:27,950 --> 00:22:30,400
What about dinner?

263
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:33,200
I don’t know when I will get off work.

264
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,300
But I know.

265
00:22:37,390 --> 00:22:38,380
How?

266
00:22:40,190 --> 00:22:41,980
When I go to see you,

267
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,700
it’s time for you to get off work.

268
00:22:49,230 --> 00:22:50,500
Do your best at work.

269
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,100
I’ve got to go.

270
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:03,800
Wait.

271
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,000
-Bye.
-See you.

272
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:28,000
I’m afraid that, about the increased budget
for personnel training,

273
00:23:28,430 --> 00:23:31,290
Madam Chanya will not agree.

274
00:23:32,070 --> 00:23:37,560
Our hotel receives high ratings
for staff services.

275
00:23:37,690 --> 00:23:44,380
I think it’s reasonable to increase
the budget for training new staff.

276
00:23:48,410 --> 00:23:49,800
About my mom,

277
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:52,100
I’ll take care of it.

278
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:54,200
What about the room rate increase?

279
00:23:54,830 --> 00:23:58,100
Due to the rising costs
and higher living expenses,

280
00:23:58,710 --> 00:24:02,650
I think we need to consider
increasing the room rate.

281
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:05,650
About that, I don’t want to do it now.

282
00:24:06,330 --> 00:24:10,400
I think we should launch a campaign
to attract customers.

283
00:24:11,810 --> 00:24:13,610
Our cost is indeed rising.

284
00:24:13,970 --> 00:24:18,800
But we can make profits from
the high quality of our rooms and services.

285
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:24,100
But I still think it’s necessary
to increase the room rate.

286
00:24:25,050 --> 00:24:26,800
All our costs have gone up.

287
00:24:28,250 --> 00:24:30,450
Miss Chan, Miss Key is waiting to see you.

288
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:38,600
Let’s wrap up the meeting here.

289
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:41,640
But we haven’t reached a conclusion yet.

290
00:24:42,660 --> 00:24:44,400
We can discuss it tomorrow.

291
00:24:45,070 --> 00:24:47,200
We’ve had this meeting for five hours.

292
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:49,610
Many of you started to feel tired,
didn’t you?

293
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:59,190
But we haven’t reached a conclusion yet.

294
00:24:59,230 --> 00:24:59,900
That’s right.

295
00:25:48,490 --> 00:25:49,500
Are you hungry?

296
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:51,400
My stomach is growling.

297
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:53,700
Let’s go find Simba.

298
00:25:54,210 --> 00:25:55,100
Simba.

299
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:00,100
Jay.

300
00:26:09,950 --> 00:26:11,300
You’re finally home.

301
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:14,000
I thought you would be alone.

302
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:18,300
I didn’t think that
you two would be attached at the hip.

303
00:26:20,110 --> 00:26:22,270
Can you stop coming to my condo?

304
00:26:23,260 --> 00:26:25,100
To be honest, what you did is illegal.

305
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,290
Now we are not together.

306
00:26:34,450 --> 00:26:36,300
This suddenly became illegal.

307
00:26:41,530 --> 00:26:42,900
Even if you were still together,

308
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:45,920
you shouldn’t come into
her room like this.

309
00:26:46,910 --> 00:26:48,200
I’m just used to it.

310
00:26:48,990 --> 00:26:51,200
I could come in here
since we were in school.

311
00:26:57,340 --> 00:26:58,600
What do you want?

312
00:27:00,180 --> 00:27:02,380
I thought this was your personal space.

313
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:06,300
So I came here to talk to you in private.

314
00:27:10,780 --> 00:27:13,000
I didn’t think anyone else would be here.

315
00:27:19,710 --> 00:27:22,400
Let’s talk when we are alone.

316
00:27:25,650 --> 00:27:27,930
This place is no longer
Chan’s personal space.

317
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,300
Right now,

318
00:27:32,620 --> 00:27:35,520
it has become a personal space
for her and me.

319
00:27:37,570 --> 00:27:39,300
If you want to talk to Chan,

320
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:41,490
you can do it now.

321
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:43,180
Chan and I,

322
00:27:44,670 --> 00:27:46,500
we have no secrets from each other.

323
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:52,800
But if you don’t want to talk,
you should leave.

324
00:28:00,620 --> 00:28:01,500
Okay.

325
00:28:03,410 --> 00:28:04,500
I’ll leave.

326
00:28:34,490 --> 00:28:35,700
You got a tattoo?

327
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:43,400
Yes.

328
00:28:49,610 --> 00:28:50,800
It’s pretty.

329
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:53,500
I like it.

330
00:29:22,430 --> 00:29:23,800
Here is your keycard.

331
00:29:32,850 --> 00:29:33,900
Goodbye.

332
00:30:03,620 --> 00:30:04,900
It’s really over.

333
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:17,300
From now on,

334
00:30:19,870 --> 00:30:21,600
you don’t need to worry anymore.

335
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:27,860
You are the only one I love.

336
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:33,640
I won’t hesitate anymore.

337
00:30:43,500 --> 00:30:45,500
I won’t hurt you again.

338
00:31:40,710 --> 00:31:41,980
You got a tattoo?

339
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:43,800
Yes.

340
00:32:36,690 --> 00:32:38,600
Jay looks terrible right now.

341
00:32:41,950 --> 00:32:43,500
What do you want me to do?

342
00:32:44,950 --> 00:32:49,180
It’s obvious that she’s trying
to get my attention.

343
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:54,900
Yes, I know.

344
00:32:57,550 --> 00:32:59,900
For the sake of our friendship,

345
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:02,700
I want you to talk to her.

346
00:33:03,390 --> 00:33:07,000
I never thought that a girl like Jay

347
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:09,530
could fall apart like this.

348
00:33:10,060 --> 00:33:11,500
What can I say to her?

349
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:13,900
She won’t listen to me anyway.

350
00:33:14,420 --> 00:33:15,900
She will listen to you.

351
00:33:16,970 --> 00:33:20,700
You are the only person in this world
that she listens to.

352
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:27,430
Jay and I,

353
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:30,200
we are over.

354
00:33:37,530 --> 00:33:39,300
You refuse to talk to her

355
00:33:41,290 --> 00:33:45,500
because you’re afraid
that it will upset your girlfriend?

356
00:33:47,410 --> 00:33:48,200
Yes.

357
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:51,900
I hurt her too many times.

358
00:33:53,310 --> 00:33:56,300
Right now, she is the only one
I care about.

359
00:33:57,670 --> 00:34:02,000
About Jay, we just need to let her
deal with it on her own.

360
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:04,200
I can’t help her.

361
00:34:19,030 --> 00:34:20,300
Here is your coffee.

362
00:34:21,580 --> 00:34:22,889
Can I have a cup of warm water?

363
00:34:22,929 --> 00:34:23,800
Sure.

364
00:34:41,429 --> 00:34:42,500
Thank you.

365
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,000
What are you doing here?

366
00:35:03,820 --> 00:35:05,300
We seem to…

367
00:35:06,910 --> 00:35:08,380
have similar tastes.

368
00:35:09,390 --> 00:35:11,980
If you’re here to pick a fight,
I’ll leave.

369
00:35:13,410 --> 00:35:14,900
I’m not talking about Chan.

370
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:21,900
Are you going to rub it in my face?

371
00:35:26,600 --> 00:35:29,370
You think I’m that kind of person?

372
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:36,000
Can’t we be friends?

373
00:35:37,650 --> 00:35:39,090
or sisters?

374
00:35:39,820 --> 00:35:40,800
Are you serious?

375
00:35:42,320 --> 00:35:43,800
Do you really think we can?

376
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:46,700
If the situation were reversed,

377
00:35:47,210 --> 00:35:49,000
if Chan and I got back together,

378
00:35:50,140 --> 00:35:54,000
would you still want to be
my friend or sister?

379
00:36:06,490 --> 00:36:08,100
I probably couldn’t do it.

380
00:36:11,790 --> 00:36:12,600
Hey.

381
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:17,000
I hate when people feel bad for me.

382
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:21,800
My life isn’t that bad.

383
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:26,100
You are acting as if you care about me.

384
00:36:28,440 --> 00:36:30,600
Is it because Chan refused to see me?

385
00:36:35,300 --> 00:36:36,700
Let me tell you something.

386
00:36:37,730 --> 00:36:40,100
Chan is right that she refused to see me.

387
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:44,200
Even if she came to talk to me,

388
00:36:47,110 --> 00:36:48,500
to take care of me,

389
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:52,500
it would make things worse for me.

390
00:37:01,560 --> 00:37:03,400
She knows me well.

391
00:37:08,590 --> 00:37:10,350
What you are doing right now,

392
00:37:11,850 --> 00:37:13,500
do you think you are an angel?

393
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,970
You must feel good to act like a saint.

394
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:22,700
I never thought I was an angel.

395
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,200
I came here

396
00:37:28,070 --> 00:37:29,540
because I thought…

397
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,900
we once really hit it off.

398
00:37:43,130 --> 00:37:45,000
Even though it was only a short time.

399
00:37:51,250 --> 00:37:53,300
If you don’t want to be my friend,

400
00:37:55,290 --> 00:37:56,600
I get it.

401
00:38:00,230 --> 00:38:02,500
Even if I move on from Chan,

402
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:05,900
you and I,

403
00:38:07,340 --> 00:38:09,100
we can never be friends.

404
00:38:13,300 --> 00:38:14,700
Just so you know.

405
00:38:16,250 --> 00:38:18,300
Your relationship with Chan,

406
00:38:19,850 --> 00:38:21,000
it will not be easy.

407
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:22,800
Be careful.

408
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:39,400
(Jay.)

409
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,300
Are you getting drunk again?

410
00:39:43,470 --> 00:39:45,000
It’s my life,

411
00:39:45,880 --> 00:39:48,200
not your business, Auntie.

412
00:39:48,890 --> 00:39:51,000
I can’t stand it anymore.

413
00:39:51,040 --> 00:39:53,410
If someone finds out
that you are getting drunk every night,

414
00:39:53,450 --> 00:39:54,700
what would I do?

415
00:39:55,140 --> 00:39:56,800
(I don’t f*cking care.)

416
00:39:58,260 --> 00:40:00,340
Don’t call me again.

417
00:40:00,380 --> 00:40:01,180
You know?!

418
00:40:04,910 --> 00:40:05,700
Jay.

419
00:40:07,010 --> 00:40:08,770
You are acting out of control.

420
00:40:38,910 --> 00:40:39,750
Sorry.

421
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:45,500
Sorry.

422
00:40:46,030 --> 00:40:47,620
It’s okay.

423
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,400
I’m sorry.

424
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:57,500
You’re finally up.

425
00:41:59,710 --> 00:42:00,800
Are you sober now?

426
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:03,400
You…

427
00:42:04,600 --> 00:42:06,100
You are confused about who I am

428
00:42:06,610 --> 00:42:08,730
and how you ended up here, right?

429
00:42:24,490 --> 00:42:25,600
Last night,

430
00:42:27,210 --> 00:42:28,260
you and I…

431
00:42:28,300 --> 00:42:30,040
Did we sleep together?

432
00:42:38,750 --> 00:42:40,100
Calm down, Miss.

433
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:43,300
I don’t like sleeping with a drunk woman,

434
00:42:43,830 --> 00:42:46,610
especially a woman who threw up
and passed out on the street.

435
00:44:08,120 --> 00:44:08,900
Hey.

436
00:44:09,290 --> 00:44:10,500
Take your money back.

437
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:14,900
Hey.

438
00:44:15,480 --> 00:44:16,500
Do you hear me?

439
00:44:36,540 --> 00:44:38,380
Here. I put it back.

440
00:44:40,920 --> 00:44:42,900
Can you slap me?

441
00:44:43,300 --> 00:44:44,240
What?

442
00:44:45,060 --> 00:44:46,000
Please.

443
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,200
Can you slap me?

444
00:44:48,830 --> 00:44:50,500
I’m begging you.

445
00:44:52,650 --> 00:44:55,570
I want to wake up. Please slap me.

446
00:44:56,230 --> 00:44:57,900
Can you slap me on the face?

447
00:44:57,940 --> 00:44:59,500
What’s wrong with you?

448
00:44:59,760 --> 00:45:02,800
-Slap me. I want to wake up.
-No, let me go.

449
00:45:03,380 --> 00:45:06,250
I want to wake up. Please slap me.

450
00:45:06,750 --> 00:45:09,300
Slap me. Slap me now.

451
00:45:12,470 --> 00:45:13,400
So?

452
00:45:13,690 --> 00:45:14,730
Did you wake up now?

453
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:17,600
Did it hurt enough?

454
00:45:25,310 --> 00:45:26,800
What the heck is this?

455
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:44,350
Hey.

456
00:45:44,740 --> 00:45:46,700
Hey, stop it.

457
00:46:31,790 --> 00:46:34,000
You threw up and passed out.

458
00:46:34,710 --> 00:46:36,360
So I had to take you back here.

459
00:46:36,400 --> 00:46:38,100
I didn’t know where you live.

460
00:46:38,460 --> 00:46:40,100
You didn’t have your phone with you.

461
00:46:45,130 --> 00:46:47,200
I’m sorry for causing you trouble.

462
00:46:49,320 --> 00:46:50,900
I’ll pay you back for wasting your time.

463
00:46:51,460 --> 00:46:53,900
Can’t you talk about
something else besides money?

464
00:46:55,160 --> 00:46:56,380
I want to make it up to you.

465
00:46:58,540 --> 00:47:03,500
I guess your life is always
revolving around money and benefits.

466
00:47:09,450 --> 00:47:11,200
You don’t need to pay me back.

467
00:47:13,030 --> 00:47:14,690
You just need to…

468
00:47:19,960 --> 00:47:21,500
leave my room.

469
00:47:23,470 --> 00:47:25,810
-Are you telling me to get out?
-You are up.

470
00:47:25,850 --> 00:47:27,570
There’s no need to stay here any longer.

471
00:47:27,700 --> 00:47:28,600
Please leave.

472
00:47:33,040 --> 00:47:34,200
What about this shirt?

473
00:47:35,990 --> 00:47:37,800
It belongs to someone I was talking to.

474
00:47:40,090 --> 00:47:41,500
But we are no longer talking.

475
00:47:42,090 --> 00:47:43,180
I don’t want it back.

476
00:47:43,540 --> 00:47:44,410
You can keep it.

477
00:47:52,400 --> 00:47:53,330
I just leave?

478
00:48:20,210 --> 00:48:21,900
-My under…
-It’s in the bathroom.

479
00:49:06,960 --> 00:49:08,700
(Let me tell you something.)

480
00:49:09,870 --> 00:49:11,900
Your relationship with Chan,

481
00:49:13,460 --> 00:49:14,500
it will not be easy.

482
00:49:15,190 --> 00:49:16,520
Be careful.

483
00:49:28,390 --> 00:49:29,500
What are you doing?

484
00:49:39,680 --> 00:49:41,500
Can I play this piano?

485
00:49:45,370 --> 00:49:46,400
Sure.

486
00:49:47,360 --> 00:49:48,810
But you need to tell me first.

487
00:49:50,200 --> 00:49:52,000
Is something bothering you?

488
00:49:58,020 --> 00:49:59,150
Yesterday,

489
00:50:00,660 --> 00:50:02,390
I went to see Jay.

490
00:50:04,890 --> 00:50:06,700
She snapped at you, didn’t she?

491
00:50:10,260 --> 00:50:14,000
You really know her well.

492
00:50:15,570 --> 00:50:16,400
Yes.

493
00:50:17,610 --> 00:50:19,370
We’ve been friends since we were young.

494
00:50:21,540 --> 00:50:24,900
But I have no feelings for her now.

495
00:50:26,760 --> 00:50:30,200
I know you love me,

496
00:50:31,940 --> 00:50:33,900
and you have no feelings for her.

497
00:50:36,250 --> 00:50:37,500
Since you know that,

498
00:50:38,770 --> 00:50:40,370
what’s the problem?

499
00:50:44,170 --> 00:50:48,900
Do you think we can make it work?

500
00:50:51,320 --> 00:50:52,300
Yes.

501
00:50:54,800 --> 00:50:56,600
No matter what problem arises,

502
00:50:58,380 --> 00:51:03,200
I will make this relationship work.

503
00:51:07,680 --> 00:51:10,000
I want to be with you like this

504
00:51:11,380 --> 00:51:12,960
until we grow old.

505
00:51:14,630 --> 00:51:18,610
Until your hair turns grey,

506
00:51:19,990 --> 00:51:21,500
you need to wear dentures,

507
00:51:22,520 --> 00:51:25,300
and you always look for your glasses.

508
00:51:26,080 --> 00:51:27,300
Do you like that?

509
00:51:28,780 --> 00:51:30,310
You really painted a picture.

510
00:51:38,260 --> 00:51:39,850
Shall we play it together?

511
00:53:00,470 --> 00:53:02,000
Sun is probably back.

512
00:53:09,170 --> 00:53:10,450
I’ll check the door.

513
00:53:18,660 --> 00:53:19,690
What’s up, Sun?

514
00:53:26,250 --> 00:53:28,000
Key, wait.

515
00:53:48,310 --> 00:53:49,200
Mom.

516
00:53:54,070 --> 00:53:55,330
How could you do this?

517
00:53:57,080 --> 00:53:58,360
Why did you get a tattoo?

518
00:53:59,510 --> 00:54:01,500
Do you think this is appropriate?

519
00:54:02,310 --> 00:54:03,400
It’s just a tattoo.

520
00:54:03,650 --> 00:54:05,560
It doesn’t define my worth, Mom.

521
00:54:05,600 --> 00:54:05,980
Chan.

522
00:54:06,020 --> 00:54:07,100
Excuse me.

523
00:54:11,150 --> 00:54:12,530
Even though she’s your daughter,

524
00:54:13,460 --> 00:54:15,160
you shouldn’t use violence with her.

525
00:54:34,690 --> 00:54:35,890
Who do you think you are?

526
00:54:35,930 --> 00:54:38,690
Do you want to show off
that you’re my daughter’s sugar baby?

527
00:54:39,660 --> 00:54:41,610
If my mom does this again,

528
00:54:41,650 --> 00:54:43,100
you need to tell me immediately.

529
00:54:43,400 --> 00:54:46,100
I like it when you protect me.

530
00:54:46,700 --> 00:54:49,890
I think Key is not a good match
for my daughter.

531
00:54:50,180 --> 00:54:53,300
She deserves someone better.

532
00:54:53,760 --> 00:54:55,450
What do you want me to do?

533
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:58,800
Do you think
you are different from your mom?

534
00:54:59,160 --> 00:55:00,120
Your mom was sick.

535
00:55:00,160 --> 00:55:01,720
How can I be sure
that you won’t have the same illness?

536
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:03,300
She is dead because of you.

537
00:55:04,170 --> 00:55:06,900
If you won’t stop talking badly to her,

538
00:55:07,130 --> 00:55:08,490
I’ll have to protect her.
